WEBVTT

00:16.684 --> 00:17.894
[Sniffs]

00:56.683 --> 00:59.102
These are the last two eggs.

01:07.360 --> 01:09.362
From my own bookshelf.

01:09.445 --> 01:12.532
Help you pass the time.
— I've already read it.

01:12.657 --> 01:16.035
You might catch something
you missed the second time around.

01:18.246 --> 01:21.082
Why did you move me
from the rec room down here?

01:21.207 --> 01:23.710
I wanted you under my own roof.

01:27.380 --> 01:30.300
Where are you keeping
your other prisoner? Miles, is it?

01:31.551 --> 01:34.971
Or you don't want to share.
— I was hoping you would share, Ben,

01:35.096 --> 01:37.598
seeing as you claimed
to have a spy on his ship.

01:42.854 --> 01:46.065
I feel for you, John. I really do.

01:46.858 --> 01:48.901
You keep hitting dead ends.

01:51.070 --> 01:55.575
You couldn't find the cabin,
you can't make contact with Jacob.

01:55.700 --> 01:59.954
You're so desperate to figure out what
to do next you're asking me for help.

02:03.291 --> 02:06.169
So here we are, just like old times.

02:06.836 --> 02:09.088
Except I'm locked in a different room.

02:12.425 --> 02:15.094
And you're more lost
than you ever were.

02:16.554 --> 02:18.598
I know what you're trying to do.

02:18.723 --> 02:20.183
It's not gonna work.

02:20.266 --> 02:23.811
Excellent, John. You're evolving.
— done with your breakfast?

02:30.193 --> 02:32.528
[Door locks]

02:46.125 --> 02:47.752
What's that all about?

02:53.466 --> 02:55.301
Mornin', ladies.

02:55.385 --> 02:58.262
Good morning. — mornin'.

02:59.263 --> 03:01.974
Hm, coffee smells good.

03:02.058 --> 03:06.145
Well, why don't I go make you a cup?

03:12.735 --> 03:14.529
Kinda weird, ain't it?

03:15.822 --> 03:19.367
Sitting on porches,
drinking coffee out of mugs.

03:19.450 --> 03:21.911
Anwvay, I found some clothes
about your size.

03:21.994 --> 03:23.788
Hung 'em in the closet.

03:23.871 --> 03:27.834
So after I kick out Hugo...
— I'm not moving in with you, James.

03:29.377 --> 03:34.048
Well... then why did you stay?
— that's none of your business.

03:34.132 --> 03:36.884
You got a secret agenda, huh?

03:37.844 --> 03:40.763
If you're spying for Jack...
— I'm not spying for anyone.

03:40.847 --> 03:43.599
Why don't you tell...?
— because I don't trust you.

03:47.270 --> 03:49.605
This is about the pregnancy thing.

03:53.693 --> 03:55.945
James. — yeah?

03:56.779 --> 03:57.822
Go home.

04:00.616 --> 04:02.243
Ok, fine.

04:03.369 --> 04:04.912
[Sighs]

04:05.788 --> 04:07.290
See you later then.

04:19.886 --> 04:21.554
You ready?

04:22.221 --> 04:23.598
Is there a back entrance?

04:23.681 --> 04:25.892
Yeah, but you're going in
the front door

04:25.975 --> 04:28.060
with your head held high, ok?

04:30.396 --> 04:32.815
Yeah. Ok.

04:34.066 --> 04:35.401
Let's do this.

04:36.569 --> 04:37.778
[Car door opens]

04:37.862 --> 04:39.614
[Man] Why did you do it, Kate?

04:39.697 --> 04:41.824
[Indistinct yelling]

04:41.908 --> 04:43.618
What was your statement?

04:46.245 --> 04:50.082
Folks, we're not making any statements
or answering any questions.

04:53.419 --> 04:55.296
[Man] Help us out here, please.

04:55.379 --> 04:58.508
[Man] The people vs.
Katherine Anne Austen.

04:58.591 --> 05:01.260
The honorable Arthur galzethron
presiding.

05:01.385 --> 05:04.931
The bailiff will read the counts.
Will the defendant please rise?

05:05.431 --> 05:08.768
Katherine Anne Austen,
you are charged with fraud,

05:08.893 --> 05:11.312
arson, assault on a federal officer,

05:11.437 --> 05:13.314
assault with a deadly weapon,

05:13.397 --> 05:16.108
grand larceny, Grand Theft Auto

05:16.234 --> 05:18.361
and murder in the first degree.

05:18.444 --> 05:20.821
Miss Austen, how do you plead?

05:23.991 --> 05:25.117
Not guilty.

05:25.201 --> 05:27.286
[Crowd murmuring]
— thus entered.

05:27.370 --> 05:28.955
I'll now hear argument on bail.

05:30.414 --> 05:33.376
Your honor, we are requesting
the defendant be remanded

05:33.459 --> 05:35.670
into custody
for the duration of the trial.

05:35.795 --> 05:38.381
My client's been free
pending arraignment.

05:38.464 --> 05:41.509
Now she's a flight risk?
— the definition of a flight risk.

05:41.634 --> 05:45.763
She has one of the most recognizable
faces. Where will she run?

05:45.846 --> 05:48.182
Miss Austen,
based on your prior history,

05:48.266 --> 05:52.144
I'm inclined to agree with the people.
You're remanded into federal custody

05:52.228 --> 05:56.065
for the duration of your trial. Bailiff,
take the defendant into custody.

05:56.148 --> 05:58.985
[Gavel slams] — sorry.

06:25.803 --> 06:28.097
"Albuquerque?"

06:31.267 --> 06:34.020
New York. — too many people.

06:34.353 --> 06:35.521
[Speaking Korean]

06:44.530 --> 06:47.825
I learn English for you.

06:50.036 --> 06:53.664
To live in america.

07:05.468 --> 07:07.470
[Woman] Hey, look! Jack!

07:11.223 --> 07:13.017
All right.

07:13.559 --> 07:14.560
[Man] Hey, man.

07:14.644 --> 07:17.897
This is... Charlotte, Dan.
— hey, welcome.

07:17.980 --> 07:19.440
[Woman] Hey. — [woman 2] Hey.

07:19.523 --> 07:23.736
Their helicopter already took Sayid
and Desmond back to their freighter.

07:23.819 --> 07:27.114
They can make arrangements
to get all of us off this island.

07:31.827 --> 07:33.412
She stayed with Locke.

07:38.584 --> 07:39.627
Hello, Kate.

07:43.047 --> 07:45.758
I just killed a chicken.

07:46.759 --> 07:48.302
What can I do for you?

07:49.053 --> 07:51.764
I want to talk to miles.
Where are you keeping him?

07:51.847 --> 07:55.059
Why do you need to talk to him?
— that's personal.

07:58.145 --> 08:01.857
And what gives you the right...
— you may think this is a democracy

08:01.941 --> 08:05.194
because of the way Jack ran things.
This is not a democracy.

08:07.488 --> 08:10.074
Then I guess that makes it
a dictatorship.

08:10.700 --> 08:14.495
If I was a dictator, I would just
shoot you and go about my day.

08:16.122 --> 08:18.416
Dinner's at 6:00 if you're hungry.

08:26.632 --> 08:28.092
Hey, Hurley.

08:28.175 --> 08:30.720
Wait. You bringing that to miles?

08:30.803 --> 08:32.847
Yeah. — Locke asked me to do it.

08:32.930 --> 08:35.182
Cool. That dude creeps me out.

08:35.266 --> 08:38.894
He's still in the rec room, right?
— I moved him to the boathouse...

08:44.900 --> 08:47.361
You just totally
scooby—doo'd me, didn't you?

08:47.445 --> 08:48.487
Sorry.

08:49.113 --> 08:52.241
You're not gonna let him go, are you?
— no. No, I promise.

08:52.324 --> 08:54.368
Just don't tell Locke it was me.

09:00.332 --> 09:03.377
[Birds chirping, squawking]

09:28.194 --> 09:30.362
So the arab traded you too.

09:40.289 --> 09:43.334
Do you know who I am?
— excuse me?

09:43.417 --> 09:45.544
Do you know who I am?

09:47.755 --> 09:49.423
Do you know what I did?

09:51.550 --> 09:53.427
What did you do?

09:54.261 --> 09:55.846
Answer the question.

10:02.978 --> 10:04.855
I'll tell you what you want to know,

10:04.939 --> 10:07.066
but you gotta do something
for me first.

10:08.234 --> 10:11.111
I'm not letting you go.
— I don't want to be let go.

10:11.195 --> 10:12.988
I am exactly where I want to be.

10:15.449 --> 10:20.746
What I want is one minute
of someone's time.

10:21.747 --> 10:23.624
You bring him to me...

10:23.707 --> 10:27.670
And I will tell you
everything I know about you.

10:34.218 --> 10:35.845
Who do you think?

10:41.684 --> 10:43.853
[Indistinct chattering]

10:51.235 --> 10:53.946
Are you ok? — yeah, fine.

10:54.780 --> 10:58.450
Listen, the da's decided
to try this case herself...

10:59.285 --> 11:02.162
Which means they're
gonna do the full—court press.

11:02.246 --> 11:04.623
We need to start talking about
cutting a deal.

11:04.748 --> 11:06.625
What kind of deal?
— my best guess,

11:06.709 --> 11:09.795
I'd say she'll take a 15—year sentence.

11:09.879 --> 11:12.840
And you serve seven. — no way.

11:14.675 --> 11:17.720
If you go to trial, you're looking
at 20 years on each count

11:17.803 --> 11:19.972
and a life sentence
on the murder charge.

11:20.055 --> 11:22.600
No.
— Kate, you confessed to your mother

11:22.683 --> 11:26.395
that you killed your father,
and now she's their star witness.

11:27.521 --> 11:30.482
What am I supposed to do?
How am I supposed to win this?

11:30.608 --> 11:32.151
Put me on the stand.

11:32.234 --> 11:34.904
And take a chance with the da
crossing you? No.

11:35.696 --> 11:38.657
Way I see it,
we've got one shot at this.

11:38.741 --> 11:41.368
What's that?
— we make it about character.

11:41.493 --> 11:44.747
Not about what you did or didn't do,
but about who you are.

11:46.165 --> 11:48.334
What do you mean, who I am?

11:49.835 --> 11:52.922
I want him in the courtroom.
— absolutely not.

11:53.005 --> 11:55.507
We need him, Kate.
It'll generate sympathy.

11:55.591 --> 11:58.636
Duncan, listen to me.
You are not bringing him in here.

11:58.719 --> 12:01.764
You want to make this about me,
my character, fine.

12:01.847 --> 12:05.893
But you are not using my son.

12:07.811 --> 12:10.105
[Chattering indistinctly]

12:10.189 --> 12:11.523
[Busy signal]

12:11.607 --> 12:14.276
Maybe we should try a number
other than the boat,

12:19.615 --> 12:21.617
[Beeps] — what's wrong?

12:21.700 --> 12:25.412
Nothing. We're just having trouble
getting a hold of their boat.

12:25.496 --> 12:29.375
You haven't heard from Sayid?
You said they left yesterday.

12:29.458 --> 12:31.126
And I'm sure they're fine.

12:33.504 --> 12:34.797
What if Locke was right?

12:34.880 --> 12:37.091
What if these people
are here to hurt us?

12:37.216 --> 12:39.218
Locke has no idea what he's doing.

12:40.094 --> 12:41.720
Then why is Kate with him?

12:46.058 --> 12:48.227
[Birds chirping]

12:52.773 --> 12:54.942
You sure he's got Ben
in his basement?

12:55.025 --> 12:58.112
Uh—huh. I saw Rousseau
take him in there last night.

12:58.195 --> 13:01.782
And does Locke ever go out?
— he's been in there cooking all day.

13:01.865 --> 13:03.659
He invited us all over for dinner.

13:03.742 --> 13:05.786
[Aaron crying]

13:05.869 --> 13:08.122
Oh, can you get Aaron for me?

13:11.208 --> 13:13.669
Just pick him up
and rock him a little bit.

13:13.752 --> 13:16.505
Um... — [gurgles]

13:17.089 --> 13:20.342
Yeah, I'm just...
Not very good with babies.

13:20.426 --> 13:22.428
I wouldn't want him
to get more upset.

13:22.511 --> 13:26.223
[Aaron gurgling]
— here, I got him.

13:30.894 --> 13:33.105
[Whimpers] — it's ok.

13:33.188 --> 13:36.358
There we go, muffin. — [grunts]

13:36.442 --> 13:37.443
There we go.

13:38.652 --> 13:40.154
You're so good with him.

13:40.237 --> 13:42.740
[Babbles] — [laughs]

13:44.408 --> 13:48.162
Just the last thing I ever thought
I'd be good at is being a mom.

13:49.747 --> 13:52.207
You know, you should try it sometime.

13:52.291 --> 13:54.626
Hey, Aaron.

13:58.964 --> 14:00.382
[Bailiff] Please rise.

14:03.802 --> 14:06.472
Court is now in session.
Please be seated.

14:13.062 --> 14:15.481
Don't fire me, ok? — what?

14:15.564 --> 14:18.734
We got killed in the opening.
I had to do this.

14:18.817 --> 14:21.028
Does the defense have a witness?

14:22.362 --> 14:23.864
Yes, we do, your honor.

14:23.947 --> 14:27.743
The defense calls Dr. Jack Shephard
to the witness stand.

14:37.628 --> 14:40.631
Your honor, I'd like to renew
my objection to this witness

14:40.714 --> 14:44.802
on the basis of relevance.
— and I'll renew my overruling.

14:45.469 --> 14:48.555
You have to be aware this witness
did not meet the defendant

14:48.639 --> 14:51.850
until after the alleged crimes
she's being charged with.

14:51.934 --> 14:54.937
He is to be viewed
as a character witness only.

14:55.896 --> 14:58.190
Proceed.
— please raise your right hand.

14:58.273 --> 15:00.692
Do you swear to tell the truth,
the whole truth

15:00.776 --> 15:02.986
and nothing but the truth,
so help you god?

15:08.951 --> 15:10.244
Dr. Shephard.

15:11.912 --> 15:15.040
Could you please tell the ladies
and gentlemen of the jury,

15:15.124 --> 15:19.044
if there are any of you who don't read
newspapers, the Internet or watch TV,

15:19.128 --> 15:21.130
how you met the defendant?

15:22.923 --> 15:25.884
On September 22, 2004,

15:25.968 --> 15:28.137
Kate, uh... [chuckles]

15:29.054 --> 15:30.639
Miss Austen and I

15:30.722 --> 15:33.058
were both passengers
on oceanic flight 815,

15:33.142 --> 15:35.936
which crash—landed on an island
in the south pacific.

15:36.019 --> 15:38.564
Were you aware miss Austen
was a fugitive

15:38.647 --> 15:42.776
being transported by a United States
marshal on that flight to Los Angeles?

15:42.860 --> 15:46.321
I did learn that eventually, yes.
— from the us marshal?

15:46.405 --> 15:48.866
No, the marshal died in the crash.

15:50.659 --> 15:54.037
I never spoke to him.
Miss Austen told me.

15:58.000 --> 16:00.377
Did you ever ask her if she was guilty?

16:00.460 --> 16:02.296
No. Never.

16:02.379 --> 16:05.174
That seems like a reasonable question.
Why not?

16:06.008 --> 16:08.886
I just assumed there had been
some kind of mistake.

16:08.969 --> 16:10.971
And why would you think that?

16:12.973 --> 16:16.435
Only eight of us survived the crash.
We landed in the water.

16:17.477 --> 16:19.605
I was hurt pretty badly.

16:19.688 --> 16:23.442
In fact, if it weren't for her I would
have never made it to the shore.

16:23.525 --> 16:26.904
[Chuckles] She took care of me,
took care of all of us.

16:26.987 --> 16:30.282
She gave us first aid, water,

16:30.365 --> 16:32.701
found food, made shelter.

16:32.784 --> 16:36.038
She tried to save the other two...
— stop.

16:37.372 --> 16:39.082
Miss Austen, please sit down.

16:39.166 --> 16:42.502
This has nothing to do with...
With anything.

16:45.547 --> 16:48.884
This is my trial, and I don't want him
to say anything else.

16:48.967 --> 16:51.803
That's fine. I have no more questions,
your honor.

16:53.222 --> 16:55.849
[Judge] Miss dunbrook, your witness.

17:00.312 --> 17:02.648
That was very moving, Dr. Shephard.

17:03.482 --> 17:06.151
I only have one question for you.

17:06.818 --> 17:09.488
Do you love the defendant?
— objection!

17:10.155 --> 17:13.867
You opened this door, Mr. Forrester.
I'm going to allow it.

17:16.161 --> 17:17.704
Dr. Shephard?

17:19.331 --> 17:21.124
Do you love miss Austen?

17:26.880 --> 17:28.840
Not anymore.

17:37.849 --> 17:42.104
So, what do you want to watch,
xanadu or Satan's doom?

17:42.187 --> 17:43.689
I'm reading.

17:44.690 --> 17:47.025
[J' Olivia Newton John: Xanadu]

17:47.109 --> 17:49.194
Will you turn that thing down?
— sorry.

17:49.278 --> 17:52.531
[Lowers volume]
— [knock on door]

17:59.997 --> 18:02.666
Hey. — can I come in?

18:04.876 --> 18:07.337
Sure. I believe you know my roommate.

18:07.421 --> 18:09.423
Hi, Hurley. — hey, Kate.

18:11.508 --> 18:14.094
You got something in your eye, Hugo?

18:15.137 --> 18:17.097
Why don't we talk in the kitchen.

18:24.021 --> 18:27.774
I know it's in a box,
but it's pretty damn good wine.

18:28.483 --> 18:29.818
I tested it.

18:29.901 --> 18:32.988
So how's life at casa de Claire?

18:33.071 --> 18:37.659
Baby Aaron keeping you up all night?
— no. He's a good sleeper.

18:37.743 --> 18:39.745
Good for you.

18:42.080 --> 18:43.123
[Exhales deeply]

18:46.918 --> 18:48.754
You are terrible at this, freckles.

18:50.088 --> 18:51.173
Terrible at what?

18:51.256 --> 18:53.842
You already said you didn't
stay behind for me.

18:54.593 --> 18:58.597
At least be woman enough to tell me
you want to use me for something.

19:02.392 --> 19:04.394
I want to use you for something.

19:05.145 --> 19:06.772
See? Wasn't that hard.

19:08.273 --> 19:11.276
[Exhales] For what? — for Ben.

19:13.445 --> 19:16.448
I want you to help me bust him out.

19:21.953 --> 19:23.663
Want to play some backgammon?

19:24.206 --> 19:25.207
You're on.

19:34.966 --> 19:36.676
Do you think I know what I'm doing?

19:39.679 --> 19:43.183
Do you regret following me out here?

19:43.266 --> 19:46.311
Are you worried about
what we should do next?

19:48.688 --> 19:52.526
All I know is I'd be a lot more worried
if I was sitting on that beach.

19:52.609 --> 19:55.070
And the rest of the group,
what are they saying?

19:55.153 --> 19:56.988
I think they're saying "baa."

19:57.322 --> 20:01.410
[Chuckles] That's the nice thing
about sheep. They're predictable.

20:06.039 --> 20:07.791
But I ain't so sure about Kate.

20:09.251 --> 20:10.877
What do you mean?

20:11.753 --> 20:12.921
[Sighs]

20:13.004 --> 20:15.715
I need your word you ain't gonna
do nothing to her.

20:15.799 --> 20:19.094
Why would I do anything...?
— just give me your word, John.

20:22.639 --> 20:25.934
You know what? Forget it.
— no, no, no. All right.

20:26.017 --> 20:28.353
[Sighs deeply]
— you have my word.

20:30.439 --> 20:32.566
She came to me about an hour ago.

20:33.358 --> 20:36.486
Said she wanted my help
busting Ben out of your basement.

20:38.196 --> 20:42.868
Why? — she talked to that guy...

20:42.951 --> 20:45.912
Bruce Lee, from the freighter,
the guy you got locked up.

20:45.996 --> 20:48.373
He told her to bring Ben down
to him for a chat.

20:48.457 --> 20:51.626
No, that's impossible.
She doesn't know where miles is.

20:51.710 --> 20:54.254
The boathouse down by the dock?

20:54.337 --> 20:56.673
If Hugo knows, everybody knows.

21:00.135 --> 21:02.471
Are you sure about this?
— yeah, I'm sure.

21:06.349 --> 21:08.894
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Where are you going with that?

21:08.977 --> 21:11.563
Whatever miles has to say to Ben...

21:11.688 --> 21:13.398
He can say to me.

21:31.082 --> 21:33.084
Son of a bitch.

21:39.090 --> 21:40.717
[Shatters]

21:47.724 --> 21:49.601
[Creaks]

21:49.684 --> 21:51.019
Come on.

22:11.081 --> 22:12.541
[Clanks]

22:18.296 --> 22:20.340
You got one minute. Go.

22:22.759 --> 22:25.804
How about some privacy?
— fifty—five seconds.

22:28.598 --> 22:31.643
You know who I am? — yes.

22:33.144 --> 22:35.730
You know who I work for? — yes.

22:35.814 --> 22:39.359
And you know he's put a lot of time
and energy into finding you.

22:42.362 --> 22:44.155
So now I found you.

22:44.239 --> 22:46.658
And I can tell him exactly
where you are.

22:49.327 --> 22:52.789
Or I can lie and tell him
you're already dead.

22:54.332 --> 22:58.545
And I'd be willing to do that
for $3.2 million.

23:01.673 --> 23:04.676
You've arranged this meeting
so you could blackmail me?

23:05.260 --> 23:07.762
It's extortion,
if you want to get technical.

23:07.846 --> 23:10.682
Three—point—two...
Why not 3.3 or 3.4?

23:15.729 --> 23:18.648
What makes you think I have
access to that kind of money?

23:18.732 --> 23:20.775
Do not treat me like I'm one of them,

23:20.859 --> 23:24.571
like I don't know who you are
and what you can do.

23:25.864 --> 23:28.700
Your friend Charlotte has seen me.
She knows I'm alive.

23:28.783 --> 23:32.245
I'll take care of Charlotte. You worry
about getting me the money.

23:32.370 --> 23:33.622
You have two days.

23:33.705 --> 23:37.626
My present situation is a little bit
restricted. Can that be amended?

23:40.337 --> 23:42.964
One week, in cash...
— time's up.

23:43.048 --> 23:45.592
Don't even think about...
— I said time's up!

23:50.472 --> 23:52.474
You got your meeting.
I want my answer.

23:55.894 --> 23:58.647
We got your name
when you called the freighter.

23:59.230 --> 24:02.275
Of course we know about you
and everybody else on the 815.

24:02.400 --> 24:05.987
Prove it.
— your name is Katherine Anne Austen.

24:06.071 --> 24:08.573
You're wanted for murder,
fraud, arson,

24:08.657 --> 24:11.117
whole bunch of other stuff
I can't remember.

24:11.201 --> 24:12.827
You're a fugitive.

24:12.911 --> 24:16.456
You were caught in Australia
and the feds were bringing you back.

24:18.208 --> 24:19.793
So yeah, we know.

24:22.087 --> 24:24.923
If I were you, I'd stay right here
on the island.

24:26.257 --> 24:28.843
Who knows? Maybe you
didn't survive the crash.

24:28.927 --> 24:31.596
Come on, come on. — [slams]

24:35.850 --> 24:36.935
[Gun cocks]

24:39.437 --> 24:41.022
Go back to your house, Kate.

24:41.815 --> 24:45.735
John, this has nothing to do with you.
— go back to your house, Kate!

24:59.791 --> 25:02.293
[J' patsy cline: She's got you]

25:07.132 --> 25:09.801
Hi. You ok?

25:11.678 --> 25:13.221
I couldn't sleep.

25:13.304 --> 25:16.391
Yeah, the beds
take a little getting used to.

25:17.225 --> 25:20.645
I didn't wake Aaron, did I?
— no. Aaron was born on this island.

25:20.729 --> 25:22.272
He can sleep through anything.

25:27.110 --> 25:31.364
What are you doing?
— I'd like a moment alone with Kate.

25:31.448 --> 25:33.658
Would you excuse us, please, Claire?

25:35.660 --> 25:37.036
It's ok.

25:41.958 --> 25:45.253
John...
— I don't need to know why you did

25:45.336 --> 25:47.922
what you did, Kate.

25:48.006 --> 25:50.800
I just need to know what they said
to each other.

25:53.428 --> 25:57.015
Miles told Ben he would lie to
the people he works for on the boat,

25:57.098 --> 26:00.226
tell them Ben was dead for $3.2 million.

26:05.023 --> 26:07.609
Listen, John, I'm sorry.

26:07.692 --> 26:11.237
I asked you where he was...
— you're not welcome here anymore.

26:12.655 --> 26:14.824
I want you gone by morning.

26:19.704 --> 26:21.247
[Door slams]

26:39.390 --> 26:42.268
I worked it out so you two
can have a few minutes of privacy.

26:42.352 --> 26:45.313
I don't need any privacy.
— you need to talk to her, Kate.

26:46.314 --> 26:48.566
I'll be outside.

26:57.075 --> 26:58.368
Hello, Katherine.

27:01.579 --> 27:03.373
Was it true, what he said?

27:06.251 --> 27:08.044
Dr. Shephard.

27:08.127 --> 27:09.629
That you're a hero?

27:19.264 --> 27:20.849
Why won't you talk to me?

27:20.932 --> 27:24.936
Because, mom, the last time I tried
to talk to you, when you got sick,

27:25.061 --> 27:28.189
when I risked my life to see you,
you called the police.

27:28.273 --> 27:29.607
Please.

27:32.944 --> 27:35.113
I don't want to fight with you,
Katherine.

27:36.656 --> 27:38.783
Why are you here?

27:43.621 --> 27:45.623
Because...

27:52.005 --> 27:55.717
It all changed,
when I thought you were dead.

28:03.016 --> 28:07.854
My doctors have given me six months
to live for the last four years.

28:08.980 --> 28:11.566
I don't know how long I'm going to last.

28:12.859 --> 28:15.153
I came here to tell you that I...

28:16.487 --> 28:19.240
I don't want to testify against you.

28:35.757 --> 28:37.759
I want to see my grandson.

28:45.350 --> 28:47.393
You came here to make a deal?

28:47.477 --> 28:50.188
Just want to meet him.

28:51.856 --> 28:53.816
I don't want you anwvhere near him.

28:58.488 --> 29:00.114
[Kate] We're finished.

29:07.914 --> 29:09.082
Oh, hey, freckles.

29:10.124 --> 29:11.668
[Lock clicks]

29:14.671 --> 29:16.089
[Grunts]

29:16.172 --> 29:17.507
You ok?

29:22.637 --> 29:25.098
Look, I'm sorry I couldn't do nothing.

29:25.181 --> 29:27.892
I wanted him to think
that you fooled me too.

29:30.478 --> 29:32.730
No sense in him
not trusting both of us.

29:35.525 --> 29:37.360
He wants me gone by tomorrow.

29:38.236 --> 29:40.613
What, he banished you?

29:42.699 --> 29:45.076
Well, I unbanish you.

29:48.663 --> 29:52.000
You can stay right here.
— [chuckles]

29:52.083 --> 29:54.585
[Grunts] This is my house.

29:56.379 --> 29:58.631
[Toilet flushes]

29:59.674 --> 30:02.468
- — Ok, me and montezuma's house.
- [Giggl681

30:04.595 --> 30:06.514
you're gonna be all right.

30:07.306 --> 30:08.766
I'll keep you safe.

30:32.081 --> 30:33.875
Time. Ok, tell me.

30:33.958 --> 30:35.835
What do you remember?

30:35.918 --> 30:38.921
Ok, queen of diamonds?

30:40.673 --> 30:43.634
Then we have the six...

30:43.718 --> 30:46.512
Of clubs. Sorry.

30:47.305 --> 30:50.433
And we have a red ten of...

30:52.977 --> 30:54.437
Hearts, maybe?

31:01.986 --> 31:04.197
It's two out of three.

31:04.989 --> 31:06.240
It's not bad.

31:06.324 --> 31:07.533
It's progress.

31:08.117 --> 31:10.828
Three cards, Charlotte?

31:10.912 --> 31:12.413
Is that progress?

31:12.497 --> 31:13.831
[Jack] Hey.

31:15.416 --> 31:17.210
I'm calling your boat all day.

31:17.293 --> 31:20.755
Why isn't anyone answering?
— we're here. How should we know?

31:20.838 --> 31:24.634
If they're not answering...
— there's only one line on that boat?

31:27.970 --> 31:31.641
There is another number we're only
supposed to use in emergencies.

31:34.685 --> 31:36.395
It's an emergency.

31:44.278 --> 31:45.530
Put it on speaker.

31:49.033 --> 31:52.286
[Beeping, ringing]

31:57.416 --> 32:00.628
[Woman] Yeah?
— Regina, it's Charlotte.

32:00.711 --> 32:02.922
[Regina]
Why are you calling this number?

32:03.005 --> 32:05.967
Minkowski wasn't answering.
The people on the island

32:06.050 --> 32:08.719
want to talk to their friends,
make sure they're ok.

32:08.803 --> 32:10.888
[Regina] What friends?

32:12.265 --> 32:14.100
[Charlotte] They left last night.

32:14.183 --> 32:16.310
Frank took them up in the helicopter.

32:16.394 --> 32:20.690
[Regina] What do you mean?
I thought the helicopter was with you.

32:39.083 --> 32:40.668
Good morning.

32:44.797 --> 32:47.967
Listen, I don't know
what you think you're doing,

32:48.050 --> 32:51.179
but you're wasting your time.
— open your mouth.

32:51.262 --> 32:52.597
Open your mouth.

32:52.722 --> 32:54.849
Wide. — [grunts]

32:54.932 --> 32:56.684
Don't talk. Bite down, bite down.

32:56.767 --> 32:58.853
[Clicks] — [grunts]

32:58.936 --> 33:01.522
I realize, when I tied you up in here
the other day,

33:01.606 --> 33:04.317
I made the mistake of failing
to introduce myself.

33:04.442 --> 33:05.610
My name is John Locke,

33:05.735 --> 33:08.863
and I'm responsible
for the well—being of this island.

33:08.946 --> 33:11.741
Eventually, miles, you're gonna
tell me who you are,

33:11.824 --> 33:14.368
and you'll tell me about the people
on the boat

33:14.452 --> 33:16.579
and why you're so interested in Ben.

33:16.662 --> 33:18.206
In the meantime, however,

33:18.289 --> 33:20.666
you're gonna keep your mouth shut.

33:22.543 --> 33:23.878
[Muffled grunts]

33:23.961 --> 33:25.546
I learned something yesterday.

33:25.630 --> 33:28.674
No use having rules if there's
no punishment for breaking them.

33:28.758 --> 33:30.218
[Whimpers]

33:30.301 --> 33:32.929
You'll be fine if you bite down
on the trigger.

33:33.012 --> 33:34.555
[Whimpers]

33:34.639 --> 33:37.308
Enjoy your breakfast.
— [muffled screams]

34:05.211 --> 34:06.712
[Gasps]

34:09.090 --> 34:10.758
[Grunts] Wait, wait.

34:10.841 --> 34:13.094
Wait. Just slow down.

34:13.177 --> 34:16.514
Oh, come on. It's not like
we ain't ever done it before.

34:18.432 --> 34:20.977
I'm cool we didn't go all the way
last night.

34:21.060 --> 34:23.771
I get it. You were sad.

34:23.854 --> 34:28.276
But, I mean, how can you resist
after that whole

34:28.359 --> 34:30.528
"I'll keep you safe" thing?
— [chuckles]

34:30.611 --> 34:32.488
No. Sawyer.

34:33.698 --> 34:36.158
What? [Gasps]

34:36.242 --> 34:38.119
What'd I say?

34:38.202 --> 34:39.704
Forget it.

34:40.204 --> 34:44.875
Oh, right. You still think
you might be pregnant.

34:46.752 --> 34:48.546
I'm not worried.

34:53.884 --> 34:55.928
And I'm not pregnant.

34:57.680 --> 35:00.641
Are you sure? — yeah, I'm sure.

35:00.725 --> 35:02.310
[Chuckles]

35:02.393 --> 35:05.354
I mean... whoo!

35:05.438 --> 35:07.815
Would it have been
the worst thing in the world?

35:07.898 --> 35:11.235
Yes! It would have been
the worst thing in the world.

35:12.069 --> 35:13.988
What would we have done with a baby?

35:15.072 --> 35:17.867
I'm going back to the beach.
— the beach?

35:17.950 --> 35:21.329
What, you're leaving?
Because of this? That's that?

35:21.412 --> 35:23.664
You crawl up in my bed one second,
the next...

35:23.748 --> 35:25.041
Goodbye, James.

35:25.833 --> 35:27.126
[Sighs]

35:27.209 --> 35:31.297
Don't make this about me, Kate. You
didn't want a baby any more than I did.

35:32.006 --> 35:35.343
You're looking for some excuse
to split, now you got one.

35:37.011 --> 35:40.473
That's all right, freckles,
I ain't gonna hold it against you.

35:40.556 --> 35:43.601
I'm just gonna sit right here
in my comfy bed,

35:43.726 --> 35:45.353
because in about a week,

35:45.436 --> 35:49.023
you'll find some reason to get pissed
at Jack and bounce right back to me.

35:49.106 --> 35:50.608
[Slaps] — [grunts]

36:00.284 --> 36:01.619
[Door opens]

36:06.874 --> 36:09.293
[Indistinct whispering]

36:12.588 --> 36:14.590
[Muttering]

36:15.174 --> 36:18.969
Got back last night, I know
which doctor she's been seeing...

36:19.804 --> 36:21.639
Miss dunbrook.

36:21.722 --> 36:24.350
Are the people ready to proceed?

36:26.102 --> 36:28.145
May we approach the bench,
your honor?

36:28.229 --> 36:29.480
Oh, please.

36:35.778 --> 36:38.406
Unfortunately, your honor,
our chief witness,

36:38.489 --> 36:41.826
Diane Jansen, the mother of
the defendant, is unable to testify

36:41.909 --> 36:44.787
because of medical reasons.
— how long will you need?

36:46.330 --> 36:47.706
I can't say right now.

36:47.790 --> 36:49.792
What I'll do is Grant a recess
for lunch,

36:49.875 --> 36:53.421
but be prepared to proceed
with your case after we return.

36:53.504 --> 36:56.424
This court is now in recess.
— [gavel slams]

36:56.507 --> 36:57.591
[Bailiff] All rise.

37:00.136 --> 37:01.846
We have to talk.

37:06.434 --> 37:10.271
My key witness spoke to her daughter
yesterday, now she's got cold feet.

37:10.354 --> 37:13.983
Quit posturing. Let's get to it.
What are you offering?

37:15.609 --> 37:16.944
Four years in.

37:20.364 --> 37:23.159
No jail time.
Kate Austen is a worldwide hero

37:23.242 --> 37:26.203
who saved five other people's lives
after a plane crash

37:26.287 --> 37:28.873
and nearly starved to death
on a deserted island.

37:28.956 --> 37:31.459
After all that,
you put this woman on trial

37:31.584 --> 37:34.545
for rescuing her mother
from an abusive husband.

37:34.628 --> 37:38.966
If you think that jury
is gonna give her actual time,

37:39.049 --> 37:42.803
then you must have
a hell of a closing, Melissa.

37:45.848 --> 37:47.183
All right.

37:48.809 --> 37:53.147
Time served plus ten years probation,
agreement she does not leave the state.

37:53.230 --> 37:55.983
What does that matter? She can...
— I'll take it.

37:56.066 --> 37:59.445
No, wait, Kate...
— give me something to sign, I'll sign.

37:59.528 --> 38:02.323
And then I walk out that back door.

38:02.406 --> 38:03.949
I just...

38:07.036 --> 38:08.537
I just want this to be over.

38:10.498 --> 38:12.583
[Melissa] I can do that.

38:12.666 --> 38:15.669
Ten years probation, and you stay put.

38:18.005 --> 38:20.424
I have a child.

38:20.508 --> 38:22.551
I'm not going anwvhere.

38:32.436 --> 38:34.438
[Sirens blaring]
— [car door opens]

38:36.148 --> 38:38.359
[Car door closes] — hey.

38:42.863 --> 38:44.698
How did you know I'd be here?

38:46.283 --> 38:50.246
Your... lawyer gave me the heads—up.

38:51.830 --> 38:53.541
He owed me one.

38:54.375 --> 38:55.543
Thank you...

38:56.794 --> 38:58.212
For saying what you did.

38:58.295 --> 38:59.838
[Chuckles]

38:59.922 --> 39:01.340
You're welcome.

39:02.299 --> 39:05.719
You know, Jack, I've heard you say
that story so many times...

39:05.803 --> 39:08.430
I'm starting to think you believe it.

39:11.308 --> 39:12.851
[Sighs]

39:12.935 --> 39:17.189
I just... I just wanted to tell you
that what I said in there...

39:20.317 --> 39:21.485
I didn't mean it.

39:29.118 --> 39:32.121
You want to follow me?
Come by for a visit?

39:33.622 --> 39:35.791
Uh... [exhales]

39:35.874 --> 39:39.003
I actually have to get over
to the hospital.

39:39.878 --> 39:44.925
But... maybe you and I can grab
some coffee together or something.

39:51.348 --> 39:54.059
I know why you don't
want to see my baby, Jack.

39:56.395 --> 40:00.482
But until you do, until you want to...

40:02.735 --> 40:06.238
There's no you and me
going for coffee.

40:08.616 --> 40:09.992
But um...

40:11.452 --> 40:13.621
If at any time
you change your mind,

40:13.704 --> 40:16.206
come and see us. — yeah.

40:29.928 --> 40:32.306
Bye. — bye.

40:32.389 --> 40:34.183
[Car starts]

41:18.936 --> 41:21.605
Kate. I'm so glad you're back.

41:23.273 --> 41:24.733
[Sighs]

41:24.817 --> 41:27.986
He missed you so much.
— did you keep him away from the TV?

41:28.070 --> 41:29.405
Absolutely.

41:30.447 --> 41:32.157
I just put him down for a nap.

41:55.723 --> 41:57.850
[Whispers] Hey, buddy.

41:57.933 --> 41:59.309
Hey.

41:59.393 --> 42:02.521
[ Yawns] — [chuckles]

42:06.567 --> 42:07.693
Hey.

42:09.862 --> 42:11.155
Hi, mommy.

42:12.406 --> 42:13.615
[Sighs]

42:14.950 --> 42:16.785
Hi, Aaron.
